# 🚀 CI/CD Pipeline Simulator

An interactive mini-project that demonstrates the basic stages of a Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipeline using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

## 📌 Introduction

The CI/CD Pipeline Simulator is a web-based educational project designed to help students understand how software moves through different stages of a delivery pipeline.

Users can click the **Run Pipeline** button to simulate the Checkout, Build, Test, Docker, and Deploy stages. The dashboard displays the status of each stage, execution logs, and pipeline history.

## 🎯 Objectives

* To understand the basic concepts of CI/CD.
* To demonstrate pipeline stages through an interactive dashboard.
* To develop a website using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
* To understand the importance of automation in DevOps.
* To use Git and GitHub for version control.
* To extend the project with Jenkins for automated checks.

## ✨ Features

* Interactive pipeline dashboard.
* Five simulated pipeline stages.
* Run Pipeline button.
* Reset button.
* Stage status indicators.
* Pipeline execution logs with timestamps.
* Pipeline execution history.
* Responsive design for different screen sizes.
* Simple and user-friendly interface.

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

| Technology | Purpose                                   |
| ---------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| HTML5      | Creates the website structure             |
| CSS3       | Provides styling and layout               |
| JavaScript | Implements pipeline simulation            |
| Git        | Tracks code changes                       |
| GitHub     | Stores and manages the project repository |
| Jenkins    | Can be integrated for automated checks    |

